<title>MEXICO: Texas to Mexico livestock export weekly - USDA.</title>
<headline>Texas to Mexico livestock export weekly - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA reported Tuesday updated figures of livestock exports to Mexico from the state of Texas to June 30.</p>
<p>Species		   Wk-To-Date   Yr-Date   Last Year</p>
<p>1) Beef Cattle</p>
<p>a.  Slaughter		281	    59,081     47,195</p>
<p>b.  Breeding Males	  11	     1,394	  838</p>
<p>c.  Breeding Females	 0	     2,594	1,227</p>
<p>Total			  292	    63,355     49,260</p>
<p>2) Hogs</p>
<p>a.  Slaughter		  0		 598     31,831</p>
<p>b.  Breeding Males	   0		 394	  249</p>
<p>c.  Breeding Females	 0	     5,109	1,454</p>
<p>3)  Dairy Cattle</p>
<p>a.  Breeding Males	   0		 156	   33</p>
<p>b.  Breeding Females     441	    15,064	6,598</p>
<p>Total			  441	    15,220	6,631</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
<p>E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
